I stand at my new door.
A door opens, and a woman comes out.
She smiles kindly at me.
"Hi," she says.
"Are you moving in?"
"Yes," I answer.
"My name is Nina," the woman says.
"I am your neighbour."
"Hello, my name is Maya," I say.
"Where do you come from, Maya?" Nina asks.
"I come from Mexico," I answer.
Nina smiles again.
"From Mexico, how exciting."
"Welcome to Denmark!" she says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
Nina is from Denmark, and she is very kind.
Now I know a person in Copenhagen.
I have my first friend.
